          <div class="border-t border-orange-100 px-7 py-8 sm:px-9">
            <div class="space-y-5 text-sm leading-8 text-gray-600 sm:text-base">
              <p>Oshima New Villa first opened here in 1975. For many years, people came to the island and filled this place with laughter. Then, with the passage of time, the property quietly closed about 15 years ago and fell into a long sleep.</p>
              <p>The buildings stood still, while the forest around them continued to grow — quietly, but with remarkable strength.</p>
              <p>When we encountered this place, what we heard first were lively birdsong and the gentle sound of leaves moving in the wind.</p>
              <blockquote class="rounded-2xl bg-orange-50 px-6 py-5 font-serif text-lg font-bold leading-8 text-gray-900">“In a city made almost too convenient, have we left something important behind?”</blockquote>
              <p>We renovated the property and gave it new life, while preserving the presence of the forest and the space to reconnect with ourselves.</p>
              <p>What you will find here is simply time moving at its own pace: the warmth of a fire shared with family or friends, and a night sky that is difficult to encounter under the bright lights of the city.</p>
              <p class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-green-900">“Sleep with the forest. Restore the heart.”</p>
              <p>We kept the name “Oshima New Villa,” the name by which this place was once loved. We hope it can become a place of renewal for you, too.</p>
              <p class="pt-2 text-sm font-bold text-gray-700">Producer, Oshima New Villa</p>
            </div>
